  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through next Friday...\n\nBroad low pressure on the lee side of the Rockies advecting\nmoisture into Montana and high pressure to our north will continue\nto bring showers and thunderstorms this evening and overnight.\nSaturday will bring continued below average temperatures in the \n70s F. High pressure to our east will advect moisture into the \nregion bringing lingering precipitation chances (40-50%) for the \nmountains and foothills. The heaviest precipitation this evening \nthrough Saturday is expected to be over the mountains and \nfoothills where there is a 40-80% chance of getting greater than \n0.5 inches of rain. Upper level flow becomes more zonal and \ndownsloping Sunday and Monday bringing more seasonal temperatures \nin the 80s F. \n\nLate Monday into Tuesday, a cold front is expected to move into\nthe region reducing temperatures into the 70s and low 80s F \nTuesday and Wednesday. Multiple waves Tuesday and Wednesday will \nbring precipitation chances to the region with Tuesday having the\nbetter chances (60-70%). Rainfall amounts are currently expected \nto be limited with a less than 50% chance for getting greater than\n0.25 inches of precipitation outside of the mountains. Ensembles\nare in general agreement that upper level troughing will then move\nout of the region and be replaced with near to above average \nheights. With this pattern in place, warmer and drier conditions \nare expected Thursday and Friday with temperatures returning to \nthe 80s and potentially 90s F (30-50%). Torgerson",
